{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392685-gods-and-the-wealth-of-nations","id":1392685,"title":"Gods and the Wealth of Nations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-29T15:22:36-07:00","id":1392685,"title":"Gods and the Wealth of Nations","content":"How strong are the ties between the success of a culture and its Pantheon in the World? Were the glory days and later decline of for example Ancient Egypt and Greece due to increasing and decreasing involvement from their respective pantheons or were these golden ages mostly due to the actions and capabilities of humanity itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:17:45-07:00","id":1392692,"title":"","content":"This strikes me as a very &quot;Every Table has an individual answer&quot; question.<br /> <br /> As for how it goes at MY table... The line is tough to draw in a lot of cases.<br /> <br /> Like, at what point do you separate the actions of the presence of a God from their worshippers? Where's the line between &quot;This was done by human hand without Gods&quot; and &quot;This was done due to Gods&quot;?<br /> <br /> Like, the Deva. The Deva are <i>everywhere</i>, and it is through their presence at all levels that the universe functions. When a poet writes amazing prose, was that purely their effort? Were they blessed by Sarasvati? Did they enter a trance state and Sarasvati guided their pen? Or did Sarasvati just let a big of her power flow into the poet to grant inspiration?<br /> <br /> I remember at one point I saw someone ask a question that amounted to &quot;If Aphrodite makes someone fall in love, is that real love or magic?&quot; to which the answer is &quot;Where does love normally come from?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ideally I'd keep it mysterious and ambiguous where the potential line of Human Action and The Divine is.<br /> <br /> Also while Gods may be more popular in some areas, I don't often tie Gods to our modern concepts of nations. Any correlation is due to demographics, not due to arbitrary lines drawn on a map that most Gods probably wouldn't think much about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-29-2020, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:10:51-07:00","id":1392849,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I suspected that the answer would be &quot;your table, your World&quot;. And that's ok I guess, I can make things up myself.<br /> <br /> I am fascinated though by what explanation the authors would have for all the different pantheons being very unevenly worshipped in different parts of the world. If the Deva are everywhere and obvious enough for Hindus to notice, would they not be noticed by all people all over the world and equally worshipped? But I suspect I need to figure this out myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:56:57-07:00","id":1392870,"title":"","content":"I think that most other gods are ACKNOWLEDGED, even if not by their worshippers.<br /> <br /> But like, even if Shiva demonstrably exists... Let's say that when at the funeral of your favorite grandparent, they were having a traditional Kemetic funeral... And nobody else seemed to notice it, but you SWEAR you saw someone who one moment was a human, and then was a jackal, and you saw your grandparent's soul leave with them.<br /> <br /> Like, yeah, the other Gods demonstrably exist. But sometimes you have ones that are YOURS. And it's a very personal, very intimate thing. One cosmology being true doesn't mean that the one you believe in is LESS true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:07:07-07:00","id":1392873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392685-gods-and-the-wealth-of-nations?p=1392849#post1392849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I suspected that the answer would be &quot;your table, your World&quot;. And that's ok I guess, I can make things up myself.<br /> <br /> I am fascinated though by what explanation the authors would have for all the different pantheons being very unevenly worshipped in different parts of the world. If the Deva are everywhere and obvious enough for Hindus to notice, would they not be noticed by all people all over the world and equally worshipped? But I suspect I need to figure this out myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming they're not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I went to church more often as a child than to temples, because I studied at Christian School.. even today I swear by Kali Krishna and Christ... In the lands of Mexico they still make blood sacrifice to the Sun God Jesus Christ, and the Kami know well that India has no mountains, because all of them moved to Japan ages ago... The idea that myths and faiths no not blend into each other and can be considered bound off into boxes is a very modern one, and not remotely applicable to even our world... How much less so then, in the World? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: And hell, Ganesha is both Deva and Yazata, how much more universally worshipped can you get <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 05-30-2020, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T15:27:56-07:00","id":1392918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392685-gods-and-the-wealth-of-nations?p=1392873#post1392873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're assuming they're not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I went to church more often as a child than to temples, because I studied at Christian School.. even today I swear by Kali Krishna and Christ... In the lands of Mexico they still make blood sacrifice to the Sun God Jesus Christ, and the Kami know well that India has no mountains, because all of them moved to Japan ages ago... The idea that myths and faiths no not blend into each other and can be considered bound off into boxes is a very modern one, and not remotely applicable to even our world... How much less so then, in the World? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: And hell, Ganesha is both Deva and Yazata, how much more universally worshipped can you get <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know lots of arguments have been made in these forums for the fact that religious people are often very broad about what different sets of gods they choose to worship, even more so in the World. This is not a reality I have experienced myself in the parts of the world I have lived (mostly Sweden and Mexico) in my encounters with religious people. So while I do not refute that this non-exclusivity exists in many places it I have a hard time believing that it is a universal, global phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Either way, that is not the point I'm making here. My wondering was why the Deva (just as an example) would have their believers mostly congregate where they do geographically if they are indeed everywhere. Were they obvious enough to be noticed by the Hindu people but not to anyone else?<br /> <br /> I fear I am going off-topic with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:11:06-07:00","id":1392973,"title":"","content":"I think in the World of Scion it very explicitly says that worship of the Gods is even more widespread than it is in our world. And maybe it's my American showing, but whilr the US is very heavily Christian territory (as the demoninations peck and headbutt) there are still people in this world we live in where people, despite not living in the regions that these religions originate in, still believe and worship.<br /> <br /> I figure it's moreso in the World of Scion. I figure the Kami may appear in Brazil, which had a massive wave of Japanese immigration, as well as the shrines built to them in any other country.<br /> <br /> The Deva manifest where their names are invoked. Anywhere. A lot of them live in what modern maps call India but those arbitrary lines were drawn pretty recently.<br /> <br /> And yes, hypothetically, Thor could manifest in Canada and get a cult formed to him by showing off. Who's to say he doesn't in the World? I figure there's pockets of worship for most Pantheons all over, and nobody finds it odd.<br /> <br /> Yes, a lot of them are more focused, but I figure that's kind of like why certain people are more widely loved in certain areas where they visited or were born in than just everywhere, despute nominal worldwide fame. I may be massively simplifying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:43:55-07:00","id":1392979,"title":"","content":"There could be Devas in the Americas. Trinidad in our world has a substantial Hindu population. At least a dozen large US cities have more than one Hindu temple. So the Devas could be in the urban USA.<br /> <br /> The Kami aren't just in Hawaii, there are Shinto shrines in California, Washington, and Oregon.<br /> <br /> Most Chinese Americans are Christian, but there are Buddhists, Taoists, and others. Thus the Chinese gods are here too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T13:48:16-07:00","id":1393192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392685-gods-and-the-wealth-of-nations?p=1392979#post1392979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Chinese Americans are Christian, but there are Buddhists, Taoists, and others. Thus the Chinese gods are here too.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's not even counting the thousands of Chinese Christian converts who are still on file, because it probably takes at least a few centuries until your records are properly disposed of.<br /> <br /> Going back to the original question, though, personally I tend to think of the history of the (mortal) World still as primarily driven by humans. And a natural part of that is that some cultures may come to worship one pantheon more or less regularly than another. Not because that pantheon is inherently better, but for any of the myriad of reasons that people both individually and as a culture adopt certain values, beliefs, preferences, etc. For instance, some gods are closely tied to natural locations (like the Netjer and the Nile), so anybody who lives around there already has a good reason to be respectful to them, maybe make a sacrifice to them now and then, and look, we've already founded a new cult! In the World, that's just common sense, really.<br /> <br /> That being said, my general view of the Gods in Scion is that they work best when they work on a) an individual basis (like blessing a single worshipper or cult), or b) a cosmic level (making sure the sun goes round and lightning is a thing). As soon as you go into the 'mid-level' stuff like social change, governments, and the course of human history, it gets messy. Because I feel like there are some seriously unfortunate implications when you think too long about the very bad things that happened to some of the cultures depicted in Scion. Like, what were the Deva up to while the British colonised India? To me, the answer is: a) they helped individuals and communities resist colonialism, and b) they made sure the laws of physics behave properly, and beyond that, err, don't think about it. There may be better answers than this on a case-by-case and pantheon-by-pantheon basis and I would love to know more about them. But we're not going to solve the problem of evil in a tabletop RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}